  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Thirty-One (Scat). Cards: 3 per hand, 3 in widow. Target: 31 pts in one suit. Logic: Sum cards of same suit. Ace=11, Face=10, 2-10=value. Three-of-a-kind=30.5. End hand: Knock (one final turn for others) or Blitz (instant win with 31).',
    Player: "Welcome to Thirty-One! Exchange cards with the 'widow' to get as close to 31 points in one suit as possible. Aces are 11, face cards are 10. A set of three-of-a-kind is 30.5! Knock when you think you're ahead.",
    objective: 'Have a hand with a total value closer to 31 than your opponents in a single suit.',
    gameplay: "1. On your turn, you may:\n   a) Exchange one card from your hand with one card from the widow.\n   b) Exchange your entire hand for all three cards in the widow.\n   c) Knock, if you believe your hand is high enough to win.\n2. When a player knocks, every other player gets one final turn.\n3. SCORING: Total up cards of the same suit. Ace=11, K/Q/J=10, 2-10=face value. Three of a kind (any suit) = 30.5 points.\n4. LIVES: The player with the lowest score loses one life. At zero lives, they are 'on the bus' and out if they lose again.",
    keyRules: [
      'Only cards of the same suit can be summed (except for three of a kind).',
      'Three of a kind is always exactly 30.5 points.',
      "A hand of 31 is an immediate 'Blitz', stopping the game instantly.",
      'If you knock and tie for the lowest score, you do not lose a life, but others do.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'From 2 to 9 or more people can play. The game is often best with 3 players but works well with a larger group.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'Standard deck, three coins or tokens per player (for lives), score sheet.',
      dealing: "Dealer deals 3 cards to each player, one at a time, and 3 cards face-up to the table (the 'widow'). Remaining cards form the stock.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. On your turn, you may:\n   a) Exchange one card from your hand with one card from the widow.\n   b) Exchange your entire hand for all three cards in the widow.\n   c) Knock, if you believe your hand is high enough to win.\n2. When a player knocks, every other player gets one final turn.\n3. SCORING: Total up cards of the same suit. Ace=11, K/Q/J=10, 2-10=face value. Three of a kind (any suit) = 30.5 points.\n4. LIVES: The player with the lowest score loses one life. At zero lives, they are 'on the bus' and out if they lose again.",
